Date: Wed, 15 Apr 2026 18:31:16 +0200
Subject: Avoid shipping the shared object at the top level.

By default we would get the following layout:

    ./usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/_lib_engine.abi3.so
    ./usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/nfstream/*.py
    ./usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/nfstream/*/*.py

That works (at least `import nfstream` succeeds) but that doens't look very
reasonable. Moving the shared object manually isn't sufficient, as it wouldn't
be possible to load it anymore.

Therefore, change its name at the `ffi_builder.set_source()` level, adjusting
the import from within engine.py.

--- a/nfstream/engine/engine_build.py
+++ b/nfstream/engine/engine_build.py
@@ -260,7 +260,7 @@ ffi_builder = FFI()
 
 
 ffi_builder.set_source(
-    "_lib_engine",
+    "nfstream._lib_engine",
     ENGINE_SOURCE,
     include_dirs=[convert_path(d) for d in INCLUDE_DIRS],
     extra_link_args=[convert_path(a) for a in EXTRALINK_ARGS],
--- a/nfstream/engine/engine.py
+++ b/nfstream/engine/engine.py
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ If not, see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses
 ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 """
 
-from _lib_engine import ffi, lib
+from nfstream._lib_engine import ffi, lib
 
 
 def setup_capture(
